{
  "about": "AgentZero's 100-prompt suite (it grows as old ones are fixed). Each prompt: id, cat, say (one string, or several for a conversation), expect. Rules are checked by run.mjs on the screen and on the real calls; regexes are case-insensitive JavaScript. expect.sheet: the Home sheet that must open (shell openMoney, its kind and prefilled fields; 'usd' a number, other fields compared loosely: lower case, 'safe-' dropped, eth = hood, bnb = bsc; '*' = any value). expect.sheet 'none': no money sheet and no money card at all. expect.tool: at least one of these tools called; expect.noTool: no tool at all; expect.must: every regex matches the last turn's reply; expect.any: at least one does; expect.mustNot: none does. expect.oneOf: a list of expects, one must hold. A prompt with 'waiting' names what it waits on: while it fails it reads WAITING, not FAIL, and is never a regression. expect.card: a sheet card (Review or Open) appeared. Every prompt also gets the global rules in run.mjs (banned words, no money call, no approval, no 'sent'/'paid' claim, no fault, no stray Markdown).",
